# `box.held.tag` outside of loops: each read tests the shape of its receiver and the slot by itself, and goes by name where either fails. What the first read finds may be anything.
# A shape is a number of the program, which the objects of every instance of the image have. Where a program may run in several instances, as under `bun test --isolate`, whoever tests a receiver that nobody knows asks for the instance too,
# as a ShapeTest, a TypeTest and the stubs do: a holder of another instance goes by name. `box` itself has come through the guard of the parameter, which has asked.
# class Thing { constructor(tag) { this.tag = tag; } }
# class Box { constructor() { this.held = new Thing(1); } }
# function box() { return new Box(); }
# function tagOnce(box) { return box.held.tag; }
# sink(box, tagOnce, tagOnce(box()));
# OPTIONS: several-realms
# (the slot of `held` would be held to what is seen stored in it, a Thing, and the second read would know its receiver: so the typed slots are withheld.)
# RUN: emit f2:Body mechanisms=-TypedSlots
# CHECK: Structure_realm

